<section class="info-hero"><div class="container py-5"><span class="info-eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</span><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>How StayNest uses and protects information when you use our accommodation platform.</p></div></section>
<section class="container info-content py-5"><div class="info-card policy-copy">
    <p class="text-muted small">Last updated: October 9, 2026</p>
    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2><p>StayNest may store account details such as your name, email address, role, property or room details, booking records, messages, and information needed to administer the service.</p>
    <h2>2. How information is used</h2><p>Information is used to operate accounts, show accommodation listings, process booking workflows, support communication between students and owners, maintain records, and protect the service from misuse.</p>
    <h2>3. Who can see your information</h2><p>Access depends on your role and the feature being used. Owners may see information relevant to their bookings and rental agreements. Administrators may access records needed to operate and support the platform.</p>
    <h2>4. Payments and sensitive information</h2><p>Do not send passwords, one-time codes, or full payment-card details through support messages. Payment information should only be entered into the designated payment flow, where available.</p>
    <h2>5. Retention and security</h2><p>Records may be retained for operational, security, dispute-resolution, and legal purposes. We use reasonable safeguards, but no online service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
    <h2>6. Your choices</h2><p>Keep your account details accurate and contact support to ask about your information or report a concern.</p>
    <h2>7. Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:Admin@StayNest.com">Admin@StayNest.com</a>.</p>
    <p class="small text-muted mt-4">This page is a general informational policy template. Review it for your organisation's actual practices and applicable legal requirements before production use.</p>
</div></section>
